+# FastLED Compatibility System
+
+This pattern editor now includes a **FastLED-compatible runtime** that allows you to write patterns using the exact same API as ESP32 FastLED code. This ensures perfect consistency between your pattern development in the browser and deployment on actual hardware.
+
+## How It Works
+
+The system provides a JavaScript/TypeScript implementation of the FastLED API, including:
+
+- **CRGB class** - Same color handling as ESP32
+- **Math functions** - `beatsin8()`, `sin8()`, `scale8()`, etc.
+- **Color palettes** - `CRGBPalette16`, `ColorFromPalette()`
+- **Fill functions** - `fill_rainbow()`, `fill_solid()`, `fill_gradient_RGB()`
+- **Noise functions** - `inoise8()`, `inoise16()`
+- **Timing functions** - `beat8()`, `millis()`
+
+## Example: Writing a FastLED Pattern
+
+Here's how you can write a pattern that works identically in both environments:
+
+### Browser (Pattern Editor)
+```typescript
+import { CRGB, fill_rainbow, beat8, CRGB_Array } from './lib/fastled';
+
+const leds = CRGB_Array(100);
+
+function rainbowPattern() {
+  fill_rainbow(leds, 0, leds.length, beat8(30), 256 / 5);
+}
+```
+
+### ESP32 (Actual Hardware)
+```cpp
+#include <FastLED.h>
+
+#define NUM_LEDS 100
+CRGB leds[NUM_LEDS];
+
+void setup() {
+  FastLED.addLeds<WS2812, DATA_PIN, GRB>(leds, NUM_LEDS);
+}
+
+void rainbowPattern() {
+  fill_rainbow(leds, 0, NUM_LEDS, beat8(30), 256 / 5);
+  FastLED.show();
+}
+```
+
+**The pattern logic is identical!** Only the setup differs.
+
+## Available FastLED Patterns
+
+The editor now includes these FastLED-compatible patterns:
+
+1. **Rainbow (FastLED)** - Classic rainbow with speed and density controls
+2. **Fire (FastLED)** - Fire2012 algorithm with cooling and sparking
+3. **Noise (FastLED)** - Perlin noise-based patterns
+4. **Palette (FastLED)** - Color palette animations
+5. **Breathing (FastLED)** - Smooth breathing effect
+6. **Sparkle (FastLED)** - Random sparkles with base color
+
+## API Compatibility
+
+### Core Classes
+- `CRGB` - 24-bit RGB color class
+- `CRGBPalette16` - 16-color palette system
+- `CFastLED` - Main controller class
+
+### Math Functions
+- `beatsin8(bpm, min, max)` - Sine wave with BPM timing
+- `beat8(bpm)` - Sawtooth wave with BPM timing
+- `sin8(angle)` / `cos8(angle)` - 8-bit trigonometry
+- `scale8(value, scale)` - 8-bit scaling
+- `random8()` / `random16()` - Random number generation
+
+### Color Functions
+- `CRGB.fromHSV(h, s, v)` - HSV to RGB conversion
+- `blend(color1, color2, amount)` - Color blending
+- `ColorFromPalette(palette, index, brightness)` - Palette sampling
+
+### Fill Functions
+- `fill_solid(leds, start, count, color)` - Solid color fill
+- `fill_rainbow(leds, start, count, hue, deltahue)` - Rainbow fill
+- `fill_gradient_RGB(leds, start, color1, end, color2)` - Gradient fill
+
+### Noise Functions
+- `inoise8(x, y, z)` - 8-bit Perlin noise
+- `inoise16(x, y, z)` - 16-bit Perlin noise
+
+## Pattern Development Workflow
+
+1. **Develop in Browser**: Use the pattern editor to create and test patterns with real-time preview
+2. **Export Logic**: Copy the pattern logic (the actual algorithm)
+3. **Deploy to ESP32**: Wrap the logic in standard FastLED setup/loop structure
+
+## Benefits
+
+- **Perfect Consistency** - Same math, same colors, same behavior
+- **Rapid Development** - Test patterns instantly in browser
+- **Easy Deployment** - Copy-paste pattern logic to ESP32
+- **Familiar API** - Use the FastLED functions you already know
+
+## Future Enhancements
+
+- **Code Export** - Automatic generation of ESP32-ready C++ code
+- **WebAssembly FastLED** - Run actual FastLED C++ code in browser via WASM
+- **Hardware Simulation** - Preview patterns on virtual LED strips/matrices
+
+This system bridges the gap between pattern development and hardware deployment, giving you the best of both worlds: rapid browser-based development with guaranteed ESP32 compatibility. 
